{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "HPLC assay method robustness (ICH Q2)",
  "notes": "Robustness study for a reversed-phase assay and related-substances method (C18, 150 × 4.6 mm, 3.5 µm; phosphate buffer / acetonitrile, isocratic; UV 254 nm). Six method parameters were varied around their nominal values in a resolution IV fraction with centre points; two columns from different packing lots were used. Each run is the mean of duplicate injections of the system suitability solution. Acceptance criteria: resolution between the API and impurity B of at least 2.0, API retention time 6.5 ± 0.5 min, tailing factor at most 1.5.",
